# Engine objects that reference a symbol only a platform object defines.
#
# The declared stack says the engine depends on nothing outside itself, so every
# line here is a violation, and together they are why engine/ cannot link alone.
#
# Down from 27: hash_bytes moved to engine/hashing.h, where arithmetic over
# bytes belongs, and the console half of misc.h moved to the shell, which turned
# three of these into honest engine-to-shell edges instead of hidden ones.
#
# 20 now: the arena seam (engine/arena.h) took the transposition table and the
# history banks off the platform allocator. The two aligned_large_pages_*
# references left in search.o are NOT the engine allocating -- they are
# platform/thread.h holding LargePagePtr<Search::Worker>, whose deleter
# instantiates in every engine TU that includes thread.h. They go with the
# ThreadPool seam, not this one.
#
# 15 now. The parallel-for seam (engine/parallel.h) took the transposition
# table's five ThreadPool references, and tt.o is free of the platform entirely.
#
# 14. get_best_thread went to the engine as Search::best_worker -- it was chess
# policy (root moves, scores, PVs, mate distance) living in the thread pool
# because that is where the workers are stored. The pool now exposes only
# worker_count and worker_at, which is mcfish worker_set.h's split: lifecycle
# and dispatch cross over, the vote does not.
#
# What remains needs injection seams rather than re-zoning:
#   Tablebases::*   the Syzygy prober, from position.o and search.o
#   NumaConfig::*   topology, from search.o
#   ThreadPool::*   from search.o and tt.o
